  <prompt>
    Author the `compose-defined-terms` capability as an Action row + Click-path Binding row (ADR-039), mirror-first under infra/dataverse/, dispatched through the shipped session-dispatch seam (NO new endpoint). The Action performs full defined-terms extraction — detecting defined terms and flagging inconsistent usage across the document — and returns `{terms: [{term, definitionSpan, usages: [{span, consistent, note}]}], inconsistencies: [{term, detail}]}` (FR-11). It is document-wide (NOT selection-based): triggered from the selection-popover "More actions…" overflow (or a small doc-level command), and its output renders READ-ONLY in the Context pane (reference display honoring the audit-only Context rule). Consumes the `compose-document` JPS scope. Ships with eval cases in task 045.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform developer fluent in JPS Action authoring, the ADR-039 Action+Binding catalog model, the SpaarkeAi three-pane Context (audit-only) contract, and OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable `compose-defined-terms` Action row (defined-terms-extraction SystemPrompt + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId) and its Click-path Binding row, authored mirror-first through the core's hoisted description source, consuming `compose-document`, triggered from the overflow menu, rendering read-only in the Context pane, returning schema `{terms: [{term, definitionSpan, usages: [{span, consistent, note}]}], inconsistencies: [{term, detail}]}` passing OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with no property-level boolean `required`. Zero new routes; eval-ready for task 045.
  </goal>

  <context>
