      Spec FR-11 + design §7 (Catalog Roster row 6, overflow trigger → Context read-only) + owner clarification (defined-terms UX = overflow-menu trigger → Context-pane read-only output). Document-wide, so it is triggered from the "More actions…" overflow (or a doc-level command), NOT the selection toolbar. Output is a reference display in the Context pane — the Context pane stays a non-input, audit-only surface (FR-28/FR-32). Note: the schema carries a `consistent` boolean-TYPE field on each usage; that is a boolean value type and is legal — it is the property-level boolean `required` KEYWORD that is banned. Consumes the R1 `compose-document` scope.
    </background>
